## Synchronizing work from a distance

Phuong: I actually have another question, because you mentioned that a part of your team is so spread out. Is there a special way or a special mode of working that you have to adapt to make it work efficiently? Because you say it's not always working, right?

Fabian: Totally. On a practical level, I think it is helping a lot that it was always like this and that its clear and fine for everybody in the team that our work setups are ever-changing and that its part of our work to question, and to react and adjust how we work together constantly. But on a personal level, and especially for me being away from Berlin and the biggest part of our team, sometimes I am a bit jealous of the social aspects and qualities that they have, working together in one space. The time together over lunch, or after work, when other topics and inputs come up. Or also just the spontaneous moments, ideating or even misunderstanding and coming to unexpected, accidental and surprising results. Those kind of things are much more touch to provoke on distance.
Or if you can be together in one place, decision making is much more efficient. If you really sit down, take your time, you discuss through it, and you call the shots. And on a distance you much more quickly start a conversation as a chat, but then the other person has something else on their mind, and it's kind of lingering.
Then again for type design it can be great to ping pong: Start an idea and then pass it on to somebody else. And then give that person some time to come back with it after they added their ideas. If that happens in the same place you much more quickly check back to see what everybody else thinks. While on distance you tend to visualise and develop ideas more to a point that is understandable without much mediation?
But in the end, for all kind of work, I think the most important thing is the communication around it: Since all we do is team work, getting everybody on board, making sure that everybody has all of the needed informations, can bring in their ideas, and so on. Obviously this takes a lot of time and energy, and is not always easy. But it is so important and it makes such a difference when everybody is connected and talking with each other. Both the process and the result.

## Communication at Dinamo

Mira: This also fits to one question we thought about. It was about which role does good communication have in effective collaboration at Dinamo? Like every one of us knows, communication is key – but we also realize that more and more in our collaborative working, especially also with language barriers. So which role has communication at Dinamo and also maybe you have tools or how do you do it on a daily basis? This thought also connected to the note on how you give critiques or feedback to each other.

